From 02e073f48abd69bb76f894724480e050657faa09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:36:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] S3-CREDITS: the parade's per-frame costs (exact): ticker
 and title plate as retained panels, no divisions, no run hash

The GBA credits parade (speed audit 3: 26.3 fps, 51 ms worst) spent its frame on work that did not change:
- look_run_hash (cross-stream: look_pool.c, called by bodyspr_image for every marcher every frame) resolved and
  hashed 21 deep fields to get 0 for every id without a run. It now returns 0 when the pool has no run for the id
  (deep_hash of an all-zero set is 0). Parade 37.4 -> 34.7 ms of work (24.1 -> 25.4 fps) on its own.
- the ticker bar is a retained panel (PANEL_OW_OBJECTIVE; its pixels change when the middle rank does), and the card
  heading is ui_title_kept(): ui_title() as a panel keyed by text, style and the sparkles' phase (new in ui.c;
  an inline ui_title() on the PS1).
- the confetti and the roadside fans no longer divide: the ARM7 has no divide, each `%` / `/` by a variable or by a
  constant in Thumb is a ~100-cycle library call (60 + 24 a frame). cr_confetti_xy() / cr_fans_xj() keep one
  remainder of the tick and running sums; the tests compare them with the old closed forms.
Exact: tests (s3_confetti_positions_match_the_formula, s3_fans_match_the_formula, the run hash with and without a run,
panel_credits_card_and_ticker_are_pixel_identical: 478 of 757 panels kept at both sizes, every frame equal with the
cache off) and 700 GBA frames of the parade without marchers hash-identical to the tip before.

